Anomaly detection
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

.. _method-provenance-autorobustanomalydetector:

``AutoRobustAnomalyDetector``
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

**Status:** robustcov composite/workflow

**Method:** Automatic robust scatter selection followed by robust-distance anomaly scoring.

**Primary references:** `Maronna et al. (2019) <https://doi.org/10.1002/9781119214656>`__, `Rousseeuw & Van Driessen (1999) <https://doi.org/10.1080/00401706.1999.10485670>`__, `Tyler (1987) <https://doi.org/10.1214/aos/1176350263>`__

**robustcov contribution:** Automatic candidate fitting, contamination thresholding, diagnostics, and end-to-end anomaly API.

**Implementation notes:** The selection workflow is package-specific and should not be interpreted as a universally optimal statistical selector.

.. _method-provenance-clusterrobustoutlierdetector:

``ClusterRobustOutlierDetector``
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

**Status:** robustcov composite/workflow

**Method:** Cluster-conditioned robust-distance detection for multimodal data.

**Primary references:** `Maronna et al. (2019) <https://doi.org/10.1002/9781119214656>`__

**robustcov contribution:** Composition of clustering and within-cluster robust scatter, with cluster-aware distances and diagnostics.

**Implementation notes:** This is an applied robustcov workflow rather than a claim of a new robust clustering theory.

.. _method-provenance-robustoutlierdetector:

``RobustOutlierDetector``
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

**Status:** robustcov composite/workflow

**Method:** Thresholded robust-distance detector built around a fitted location/scatter estimator.

**Primary references:** `Rousseeuw & Van Driessen (1999) <https://doi.org/10.1080/00401706.1999.10485670>`__, `Maronna et al. (2019) <https://doi.org/10.1002/9781119214656>`__

**robustcov contribution:** Estimator cloning, contamination/quantile thresholding, score API, diagnostics, and sklearn-compatible behavior.

**Implementation notes:** This is a package workflow over established robust Mahalanobis-distance ideas.

Cellwise covariance
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

.. _method-provenance-cellmcd:

``CellMCD``
^^^^^^^^^^^

**Status:** Literature-based adaptation

**Method:** Cellwise minimum covariance determinant estimation with mask updates and missing-data EM steps.

**Primary references:** `Raymaekers & Rousseeuw (2024) <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.2023.2267777>`__

**robustcov contribution:** Independent implementation, grouped support-pattern solves, diagnostics, corrected-data transforms, and performance gates.

**Implementation notes:** The package follows the CellMCD objective while using implementation-specific initialization and numerical safeguards.

**Public aliases:** ``CellwiseMinimumCovarianceDeterminant``, ``CellwiseMCD``

.. _method-provenance-cellrcov:

``CellRCov``
^^^^^^^^^^^^

**Status:** Literature-based adaptation

**Method:** High-dimensional covariance estimation under mixed casewise/cellwise contamination and missingness.

**Primary references:** `Centofanti et al. (2025) <https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.19925>`__, `Centofanti et al. (2026) <https://doi.org/10.1080/00401706.2026.2643216>`__

**robustcov contribution:** Integration with CellPCA, score-space robust scatter, shrinkage selection, complete covariance output, and diagnostics.

**Implementation notes:** The implementation is based on the public CellRCov description and is not claimed to be numerically identical to reference research code.

**Public aliases:** ``CellwiseRegularizedCovariance``, ``CellwiseRobustCovariance``

Distributionally robust principal components
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

.. _method-provenance-distributionallyrobustpca:

``DistributionallyRobustPCA``
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

**Status:** Literature-based adaptation

**Method:** Weighted-Wasserstein PCA with anisotropic transport geometry and exact or surrogate worst-case reconstruction criteria.

**Primary references:** `Xu, Wood & Yang (2026) <https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.10463>`__, `Wang, Liu & Chen (2025) <https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.02494>`__

**robustcov contribution:** Experimental exact-dual candidate evaluation, deterministic adaptive-geometry path search, scale-equivariant geometry normalization, sklearn-compatible API, diagnostics, and shift-focused benchmarks.

**Implementation notes:** The default exact formulation minimizes the genuine weighted-Wasserstein worst-case risk over a finite deterministic candidate path, not over the entire Grassmann manifold. The sqrt-n radius is a transparent heuristic rather than the full RWPI calibration from Xu, Wood, and Yang.

**Public aliases:** ``WassersteinRobustPCA``

